{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516349-v5-harbingers-not-entirely-sure-on-the-lore","id":1516349,"title":"(V5) Harbingers...not entirely sure on the lore.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-27T09:44:57-07:00","id":1516349,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> (V5) Harbingers...not entirely sure on the lore.","content":"I don't know if this is addressed in Cults of the Blood Gods or not (and I don't have access to the book yet to find out for myself), but I'm confused and trying to reconcile some things for myself regarding the Harbingers.<br /> <br /> Joined the Hecata, the ones who claimed to join the Sabbat ditched them like a bad habit, replaced their nasty-ass flaw for the painful kiss, still chasing their blood vendetta but keeping it on the DL for now, not subject to the Beckoning. Loresheet confirms some percentage of them actually did devolve to wraiths, and &quot;procured&quot; shiny new vampire bodies to terrorize the Skinlands once again. Got all that.<br /> <br /> The v5 content I've seen seems to have conveniently left out they're all methuselahs, and they don't embrace. So, my question: is &quot;recruitment&quot; open, or are they still in the process of reincorporation? 6th-8th generation fledglings running around hardly seems prudent and would pose more of a vulnerability than anything, and contrary to the themes and general depowering 5th edition puts on the forefront. Are they ganking other clans' or bloodlines' neonates, burning out those pesky souls, and shoving wraiths into the bodies for &quot;childer&quot; of appropriate generation?<br /> <br /> If an Hecata of another bloodline pulled that stunt, would the result be eligible for the Harbinger loresheet? Would that be a stunt Harbingers would endorse, or would they drop the hammer for doing it? Would this not be the single nastiest sect infiltration tactic this side of Vicissitude and Dominate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-27T10:28:56-07:00","id":1516351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516349-v5-harbingers-not-entirely-sure-on-the-lore#post1516349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Loresheet confirms some percentage of them actually did devolve to wraiths, and &quot;procured&quot; shiny new vampire bodies to terrorize the Skinlands once again. Got all that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it is not entirely clear those Harbringers are indeed &quot;agents of the Hierarchy&quot; and indeed Wraiths in a vampire body or just delusional and belive themselves to be wraiths in vampire bodies...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516349-v5-harbingers-not-entirely-sure-on-the-lore#post1516349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm confused and trying to reconcile some things for myself regarding the Harbingers.<br /> <br /> Joined the Hecata, the ones who claimed to join the Sabbat ditched them like a bad habit, replaced their nasty-ass flaw for the painful kiss</div> </div> </div> </div>It is... better not overthink it, when it comes to V5 or you soon realize how totally insane the whole idea, joining/forming the Hecata regrew the skin of a Harbringer flayed from their skull, the Samedi &quot;got better&quot; from their rotten corpse state (it is not a phase mooooom) and the Cappadocian lost theri deathly palor, while the Nagaraja their shark-like teeth...<br /> <i>But if we can accept </i>all that above?<br /> Suspension of belief is strong<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516349-v5-harbingers-not-entirely-sure-on-the-lore#post1516349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The v5 content I've seen seems to have conveniently left out they're all methuselahs, and they don't embrace.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> The answer to this lies in The Black Hand: A Guide to the Tal'Mahe'Ra actually<br /> The book revealed, the Harbringers of Skulls actually had two faction<br /> One that joined the Sabbat (In truth, while they are nominally Sabbat members, they merely seek allies in their vendetta against the Giovanni and the Camarilla clans who betrayed them.) is a cabal of a bit pissed of Harbringers who refuse to Embrace and they are quite potent in blood<br /> ...and the Harbringers of the Tal'Mahe'Ra<br /> The Harbingers of the Tal'mahe'Ra are more interested in studying and exploring the Underworld than in revenge. Even so, they too have availed themselves of the chance to return to the Skinlands, many creating ghouls and Embracing childer to help them function outside of the Underworld.<br /> <br /> Capuchin is more than one individual: Japheth (who has been a wraith for over five centuries since his incomplete diablerie), Lazarus and Byzar who together make up the Cult of the Capuchin and this little fact makesthe whole matter way more complicated, since the Capuchin is known by the several different bloodlines that have formed the Hecata:<br /> To the Harbingers, he is a savior<br /> To the Samedi, a rival and confidante of the Baron<br /> To the Giovanni, he is either a demon come to hurry them, or a dealer in antiquities who once traded Vatican tomes and secrets for necromantic ones<br /> Yet he/it is essentially acting as the Hecata <i>de facto</i> leader.<br /> <br /> Personally the Hecata is such a headache (like most of the V5) it takes a time and dedicated effort to untangle the gordian knots and as I said a tons of suspension of belief and...<br /> ...well just not overthing it and ask questions ,becasue the answers are more confusing than the unknown\u200b<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-27T11:50:21-07:00","id":1516356,"title":"","content":"I ignored it and had them return the Sabbat following the family reunion along with the milliners. Loosely speaking they form the heceta antitribu .<br /> <br /> <br /> I tend to treat the concept of heceta as more a way of saving face by letting everyone claim the prestige of bring a clan combined witn a series of non aggression pacts with the capuchin in charge in a &quot;do as I command or I'll kill you.&quot;/mediator way. The harbingers stuck with the Sabbat as a matter of convenience since they're utterly disconnected with humanity and they'd built up a lot of personal power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 06-27-2023, 03:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-27T13:13:16-07:00","id":1516359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516349-v5-harbingers-not-entirely-sure-on-the-lore?p=1516351#post1516351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is... better not overthink it, when it comes to V5 or you soon realize how totally insane the whole idea, joining/forming the Hecata...</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm personally fine with that, the Cappadocians' clan flaw has always been depicted as...mutable, subject to the wiles of time, Road/Path rating, lineage, or apparently Ashur's personal opinion even post-diablerie. <i>Then</i> came Lamia's curse, and everything afterwards; the notion present representatives agreed to take on the curse of Lamia at the Family Reunion doesn't lack credibility, as far as I'm concerned.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200b<br /> The answer to this lies in The Black Hand: A Guide to the Tal'Mahe'Ra actually<br /> \u200b </div> </div> </div>If it were only that simple. V20's metaplot-agnostic, and that book in particular has to assume the Sixth Great Maelstrom never occurred simply to exist and have plot relevance. V5's a metaplot continuation, even if leaves the goofier and irrelevant parts of the Week of Nightmares and Sixth Great Maelstrom by the wayside. The v5 books imply the Sixth Great Maelstrom occurred in <i>some</i> fashion, just by stating the Nagaraja who attended the Reunion were refugees of some catastrophe which hit Enoch. I don't know if any of the v5 books state outright if any extant Harbingers were members of the Tal'Mahe'Ra -- but there's certainly room for it.<br /> <br /> But with that said, while I can see it I'm personally not a fan of the Capuchin being a shared alternate identity between three Cappadocian methuselahs. Especially three of varying levels of butthurt over the Feast of Folly and Cappadocius' diablerie, who apparently for some reason by their powers combined have created Captain Gehenna.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516349-v5-harbingers-not-entirely-sure-on-the-lore?p=1516356#post1516356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tend to treat the concept of heceta as more a way of saving face by letting everyone claim the prestige of bring a clan combined witn a series of non aggression pacts with the capuchin in charge in a &quot;do as I command or I'll kill you.&quot;/mediator way. The harbingers stuck with the Sabbat as a matter of convenience since they're utterly disconnected with humanity and they'd built up a lot of personal power.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually like the Hecata. For all the various clans that have torn themselves apart, reformed, and/or went their separate ways with only disclaimed lineage being a common vein, it's kind of fun seeing a clan in diaspora trying to rebuild itself. Especially when that clan is one historically known for its Antediluvian burning it all to the ground and starting over when things didn't go their way, and for that reason that clan managed all three of the above.<br /> <br /> The implication this is Cappadocius going &quot;third time's the charm!&quot; from...somewhere...is too amusing to ignore.<br /> <br /> But ultimately, this boils down to me as one part of the clan saying &quot;we're fucked when the Promise expires&quot;, another part saying &quot;the Jyhad is getting too weighty for us to stay independent&quot;, and a third saying &quot;fuck it, let's burn it all down&quot;, and everyone realizing going their own way isn't working -- and never really did to begin with. So, better to stick together at least for now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 06-27-2023, 04:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-27T15:45:47-07:00","id":1516369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516349-v5-harbingers-not-entirely-sure-on-the-lore#post1516349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The v5 content I've seen seems to have conveniently left out they're all methuselahs, and they don't embrace. So, my question: is &quot;recruitment&quot; open, or are they still in the process of reincorporation? 6th-8th generation fledglings running around hardly seems prudent and would pose more of a vulnerability than anything, and contrary to the themes and general depowering 5th edition puts on the forefront. Are they ganking other clans' or bloodlines' neonates, burning out those pesky souls, and shoving wraiths into the bodies for &quot;childer&quot; of appropriate generation?</div> </div> </div> </div>For now there's just a lot speculation but more or less that's what I'm speculating. I speculated on this a bit in the Lazarus thread I made earlier this year. I don't think that the Harbringers are capable of siring children. They're dead-dead in a way that normal vampires aren't. They get the bodies of other vampires and shove the wraith-soul of one of the Cappadocians that was trapped in Kaymakli into the body, allowing it to animate and control it. Mechanically they're mostly vampires, but a little different.<br /> <br /> Taking the speculation a step further, these wraith-souls need to possess the body of someone with the same bloodline that they had in life. So the Harbingers, as Cappadocians, need to possess the bodies of vampires with Cappadocian blood - the Giovanni. The Harbringers never really had a feud, per se, with the Giovanni, they just needed Giovanni bodies to possess. With the Family Reunion, there's now a whole lot Cappadocian-descended vampires all hanging out together, which makes it really easy for the Harbringers to gain access to new bodies to help their wraithly brethren that are still trapped in the Underworld. It also seems very likely that Lazarus knows exactly what the Harbringers are doing and is supporting them.<br /> <br /> In prior editions, Lazarus was noted as attempting to recreate the Spell of Life (the magical spell that Osiris used to create the Mummies). Lazarus spent time with the Followers of Set in an attempt to unravel this spell. It's possible that the creation of Harbringers (wraiths possessing and becoming vampires) could possibly be a step in that process as a Harbringer is something that is a little bit close to a Mummy in some respects.<br /> <br /> What this means is that at some point the Hecata are likely to implode when the other factions realize that the Harbringers are hunting them down, likely with the assistance of Lazarus. At that point you'll probably see a war within the Hecata between the Harbringers and everyone else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-27T16:52:20-07:00","id":1516377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516349-v5-harbingers-not-entirely-sure-on-the-lore?p=1516359#post1516359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I actually like the Hecata. For all the various clans that have torn themselves apart, reformed, and/or went their separate ways with only disclaimed lineage being a common vein, it's kind of fun seeing a clan in diaspora trying to rebuild itself. Especially when that clan is one historically known for its Antediluvian burning it all to the ground and starting over when things didn't go their way, and for that reason that clan managed all three of the above.<br /> <br /> The implication this is Cappadocius going &quot;third time's the charm!&quot; from...somewhere...is too amusing to ignore.<br /> <br /> But ultimately, this boils down to me as one part of the clan saying &quot;we're fucked when the Promise expires&quot;, another part saying &quot;the Jyhad is getting too weighty for us to stay independent&quot;, and a third saying &quot;fuck it, let's burn it all down&quot;, and everyone realizing going their own way isn't working -- and never really did to begin with. So, better to stick together at least for now.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I find them a little dull, the individual bloodlines of the clan are more compelling than the concept of a hecata as a sort of Cappadocian but more of an archeotype than culture as per v5s preferences. Id be genuinely bemusee by someone playing a hecata minus/over the bloodlines but someone at oynx path was smart enough to realise you could have your cake and eat it with what we got so everyone won here.<br /> <br /> They really should have had them do all the writting when white wolf was dissolved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 06-27-2023, 07:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-27T18:19:50-07:00","id":1516397,"title":"","content":"Funny thing for me is that the Harbingers of Skulls' version i use ain't even canon anymore, but the ones from the original blurb in Pochtli's writeup in Clanbook: Giovanni, who seemed to be far more of a regional (possibly pre-columbian) power and as much of a threat, if not more, to the Sabbat in Mexico and Central America as to the Giovanni in general or the Pisanob in particular.<br /> <br /> And to be completely honest that would be proably be the least of the problems with trying to use anything related to the Hecata in my games - damn, in one particular chronicle i even threw a monkeywrench of a retcon of the Giovanni <b>not</b> descending from Cappadocians <b>at all</b> and tales claiming either such a relation or a pogrom on the Giovanni's part being simply half a millenia of rampant rumour-mongering and misinterpretation of a few specific events (mostly involving Genevra and/or Ambrogino 'siccing agents of the Caps to them stealthily purloin the remnants necromantic secrets).<br /> <br /> Cappadocians were gone due to their own religious &amp; philosophical manias leading to the greater part of the clan maintainig their havens and herds in the midst of churchs, monasteries and nunneries, of all places to be when the Inquisition kickstarts.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-01T19:23:37-07:00","id":1516938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516349-v5-harbingers-not-entirely-sure-on-the-lore#post1516349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if this is addressed in Cults of the Blood Gods or not (and I don't have access to the book yet to find out for myself), but I'm confused and trying to reconcile some things for myself regarding the Harbingers.<br /> <br /> Joined the Hecata, the ones who claimed to join the Sabbat ditched them like a bad habit, replaced their nasty-ass flaw for the painful kiss, still chasing their blood vendetta but keeping it on the DL for now, not subject to the Beckoning. Loresheet confirms some percentage of them actually did devolve to wraiths, and &quot;procured&quot; shiny new vampire bodies to terrorize the Skinlands once again. Got all that.</div> </div> </div> </div>First off, the Harbingers were never really all that loyal to the Sabbat. More like allies of convenience and once the Sabbat started going really off the reservation while some new opportunities arose for them with what would become the Hecata, they jumped ship. In fact of all the Bloodlines that make up the Hecata, the Harbingers have probably gotten the most out of the whole thing. They've gotten as much of their revenge as they could, regained the ability to Embrace and now sit as one of the three most powerful Bloodlines in the Clan. So much so that at least of them are pushing for greater prohibitions against vendetta murders within the Clan.<br /> <br /> There was also the involvement of the Capuchin (aka Lazarus or a triumvirate of Lazarus, Byzar and the wraith of Japheth) in these events whom the Harbingers of Skull are deeply indebted to as the Capuchin was the one that got them out of the Underworld. Some out right see him as their savior. So it's rather unsurprising that if the Capuchin said to join the Hecata, most if not all would do so.<br /> <br /> In fact the whole Giovanni Uprising and Family Reunion were almost certainly engineered by the Capuchin who is pretty much the de facto head of the Clan now. And while it is never confirmed, it is hinted at that why the Bloodlines of Death lost their unique flaws and gained the Giovanni one (as well as the Harbingers of Skull regaining their ability to Embrace) is because Augustus was sacrificed in a ritual to weld the Bloodlines back together (well barring the Nagaraja as they can't actually trace their origins to the original Clan of Death), presumably enacting by the Capuchin.<br /> <br /> As for why they aren't subjected to the Beckoning, it's all the Hecata, not just the Harbingers and nobody knows why. The popular theories are that with Cappadocius, Augustus and all the other Elders of the Clan are either dead or a part of the Hecata, there's no one of their Blood to Beckon them. The other is that it's effect of the Capuchin's aforementioned ritual.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516349-v5-harbingers-not-entirely-sure-on-the-lore#post1516349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The v5 content I've seen seems to have conveniently left out they're all methuselahs, and they don't embrace. So, my question: is &quot;recruitment&quot; open, or are they still in the process of reincorporation? 6th-8th generation fledglings running around hardly seems prudent and would pose more of a vulnerability than anything, and contrary to the themes and general depowering 5th edition puts on the forefront. Are they ganking other clans' or bloodlines' neonates, burning out those pesky souls, and shoving wraiths into the bodies for &quot;childer&quot; of appropriate generation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, the Harbingers can now Embrace as normal again. It was never clear why exactly they couldn't Embrace before though it has been suggested it was a side effect of being trapped in the Underworld for centuries.<br /> <br /> As for Generation, V5 has kind of mechanically walked away from it for Blood Potency akin to VtR. Also, Generation doesn't automatically create more powerful Fledglings, rather it raises the limitations on the power they can develop. An 8th Gen Fledgling will be as powerful as an 11th Gen. The 8th Gen just has a higher cap on that power but they still have to work to get to that level. That's the reason why [Tremere] and Augustus were never on the level of the original 13th Gen.<br /> <br /> As for Harbinger reproduction, as you point out, while some are wraiths, they are inhabiting vampire bodies. So when they Embrace, it's the vampire blood in their bodies that is doing the Embrace so they Embrace as normal because it's the Vitae of the vampire that causes the Embrace, not the soul of the vampire. To the best of my knowledge there isn't a means to readily replicate the Wraith-Harbingers among the original Harbingers of Skull.<br /> <br /> The closest we get is an Oblivion Ritual that allows one to put a wraith into a corpse and the apparent resurrection of the Cappadocian Constancia. However both involved mortal corpses, not vampires. And it's not certain if Contancia was actually Constancia or someone/something else.<br /> <br /> It should also be noted that among the Harbingers there is a question as to whether or not Wraith-Harbingers are an actual thing or if those Harbingers are merely deluding themselves due to the memory loss and mental trauma sustained during their centuries in the Underworld. In fact, that loresheet is the only part of CotBG that actually brings up that notion of Wraith-Harbingers. The actual section discussing the Harbinger Bloodline doesn't mention them at all. It regards the Harbingers as purely vampires.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516349-v5-harbingers-not-entirely-sure-on-the-lore#post1516349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If an Hecata of another bloodline pulled that stunt, would the result be eligible for the Harbinger loresheet? Would that be a stunt Harbingers would endorse, or would they drop the hammer for doing it? Would this not be the single nastiest sect infiltration tactic this side of Vicissitude and Dominate?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mechanically no. CotBG straight up says that you can only possess one Bloodline Loresheet per PC. And again, there is no explained method for doing that kind of thing.<br /> <br /> Besides, the Clan of Death has long known how to use wraiths as spies on their fellow Kindred. Hell, their monopoly on Necromancy has grown since becoming the Hecata so there are far less reasons to go to more extreme measures like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-01T23:46:22-07:00","id":1516947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516349-v5-harbingers-not-entirely-sure-on-the-lore?p=1516938#post1516938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for why they aren't subjected to the Beckoning, it's all the Hecata, not just the Harbingers and nobody knows why. The popular theories are that with Cappadocius, Augustus and all the other Elders of the Clan are either dead or a part of the Hecata, there's no one of their Blood to Beckon them. The other is that it's effect of the Capuchin's aforementioned ritual.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as the now-universal flaw, my suspicion is that Lazarus just ate Uncle Augie and dictated the new flaw. The Cappadocians' flaw has always been more...fluid...than that of other clans, for some reason. Whether that's dark ages Cappadocians who preemptively had horrific visage (as in the clan-specific 3-point flaw), Cappadocian bloodlines having flaws all over the place, the Lamiae being able to subvert Augustus' control over his own lineage to curse them with the painful Kiss, the premascine Giovanni retaining the old flaw, the original flaw worsening after Cappadocius' diablerie, and god knows what else in between.<br /> <br /> Crazier crap has happened, and vampires at 5th generation and below are entirely capable of single-handedly asserting -- and breaking -- curses that affect entire lineages.<br /> <br /> The answer to the Beckoning is probably simple enough: like you said, there aren't very many Cappadocian-lineage methuselahs left to do any Beckoning, and the ones who are probably are disinclined to do it. Assuming the Reunion wasn't a Beckoning of and by itself, and the Nagaraja just caught wind of it and tagged along because they needed allies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again, the Harbingers can now Embrace as normal again. It was never clear why exactly they couldn't Embrace before though it has been suggested it was a side effect of being trapped in the Underworld for centuries. </div> </div> </div>I don't recall any pre-v5 sources that outright state they <i>couldn't</i> embrace, just that they weren't and weren't offering it. That doesn't necessarily imply they weren't capable by its own, given how reluctant elders and methuselahs are to embrace in modern nights.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for Generation, V5 has kind of mechanically walked away from it for Blood Potency akin to VtR. Also, Generation doesn't automatically create more powerful Fledglings, rather it raises the limitations on the power they can develop. An 8th Gen Fledgling will be as powerful as an 11th Gen. The 8th Gen just has a higher cap on that power but they still have to work to get to that level. That's the reason why [Tremere] and Augustus were never on the level of the original 13th Gen. </div> </div> </div>Generation in v5 does automatically create more powerful fledglings: vampires of 9th and lower have minimum blood potencies of 2 or more. For that, the situation for that is actually worse than it was prior to v5 as blood potency impacts the ability to use and resist <i>any</i> discipline, and not just Dominate and Presence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It should also be noted that among the Harbingers there is a question as to whether or not Wraith-Harbingers are an actual thing or if those Harbingers are merely deluding themselves due to the memory loss and mental trauma sustained during their centuries in the Underworld. In fact, that loresheet is the only part of CotBG that actually brings up that notion of Wraith-Harbingers. The actual section discussing the Harbinger Bloodline doesn't mention them at all. It regards the Harbingers as purely vampires. </div> </div> </div>We should clear up what we're calling a &quot;Wraith-Harbinger&quot;.<br /> <br /> If we're talking about the old fucks that survived the Feast of Folly and kicked around in the Shadowlands for however long, that's absolutely a thing and it's pretty clear from past-edition lore they at least needed a corpse on this side of the Shroud to possess. They didn't have Nihilistics/Vitreous path initially to sustain themselves on wraiths, and once the initial supply ran out, that was it for them and they devolved. <i>How</i> that happened, and the implications it had for the Harbingers' existence (AKA, how they retained generation, disciplines, et cetera), was less clear-cut and this is the first time (I can recall) we got anything approaching mechanics for it.<br /> <br /> I know v20 has that band-aid solution about Harbingers sustaining themselves off the river Styx or however that worked, and of course there was always Enoch and its imported kine (which was always a bit silly if you ask me). But, those aren't all-encompassing solutions and v20 is best considered a side game/alternate timeline to v5 with its built-in metaplot agnosticism.<br /> <br /> Now, if we're talking about taking <i>actual</i> wraiths as opposed to disembodied vampires, that's where I'm looking in terms of Harbinger &quot;reproduction&quot;. If this is a thing they can just do now, it seems like it would be a preferable alternative to the embrace: you're getting a product already bound to you in a way not easily replicable without decades of thralldom and conditioning, in a package that isn't essentially a free meal for your enemies, without having to put your blood out there for anyone with sorcery to track and weaponize against you.<br /> <br /> <i>(Assuming the handful of discipline levels, sorcery paths, and rituals that allow for attacking a vampire's sire through blood sympathies ever get reprinted for v5...)</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-02T02:12:00-07:00","id":1516957,"title":"","content":"In my cannon I just treated them as Cappadocian survivors the convoluted Wraith stuff didn't matter since you can't play them anyway and they're not going to tell you in game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-02T09:55:48-07:00","id":1516976,"title":"","content":"I admit I like the subversion of the Harbingers and Giovanni versus the Salubri and Tremere.<br /> <br /> Harbingers: &quot;WE WILL DESTROY YOU ALL BECAUSE OF THE ACTIONS OF AUGUSTUS GIOVANNI!&quot;<br /> <br /> *pause*<br /> <br /> Giovanni: :&quot;But we all HATE Augustus Giovanni.&quot;<br /> <br /> Harbingers: Oh. You want to team up?<br /> <br /> Giovanni: YES.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-02T10:02:39-07:00","id":1516977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516349-v5-harbingers-not-entirely-sure-on-the-lore?p=1516947#post1516947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As far as the now-universal flaw, my suspicion is that Lazarus just ate Uncle Augie and dictated the new flaw. The Cappadocians' flaw has always been more...fluid...than that of other clans, for some reason. Whether that's dark ages Cappadocians who preemptively had horrific visage (as in the clan-specific 3-point flaw), Cappadocian bloodlines having flaws all over the place, the Lamiae being able to subvert Augustus' control over his own lineage to curse them with the painful Kiss, the premascine Giovanni retaining the old flaw, the original flaw worsening after Cappadocius' diablerie, and god knows what else in between.<br /> <br /> Crazier crap has happened, and vampires at 5th generation and below are entirely capable of single-handedly asserting -- and breaking -- curses that affect entire lineages.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. After all in previous Editions, Giovanni PC could take the Cappa Flaw instead of the Giovanni one. And some of the earliest members of the Clan had the Cappa Flaw instead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516349-v5-harbingers-not-entirely-sure-on-the-lore?p=1516947#post1516947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't recall any pre-v5 sources that outright state they <i>couldn't</i> embrace, just that they weren't and weren't offering it. That doesn't necessarily imply they weren't capable by its own, given how reluctant elders and methuselahs are to embrace in modern nights.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Guide to the Sabbat (which I believe is their first official write-up) says that they haven't Embraced since joining the Sabbat and that they are ancient. Further it has a textbox that emphasizes that they aren't really meant to be playable outside of elder games due to all of them being of low generation and advanced age. The V20 Rulebook doesn't say one way or the other while LotB takes the stance that at least some are able to but either don't because Lazarus forbade to or do so in secret. Probably because they realized that by giving them a splat entry back GotS, people are going to play them as given what they are prior to V5, the Harbingers really seem like an NPC Bloodline outside of Elder Games. So might as well give the players the tools to play younger Harbingers.<br /> <br /> It's also a bit muddied in V5 due to the Harbingers of Ashur not just being the Harbingers of Skull but a number of surviving Cappadocians that joined them. Chief among them being Roger de Camden who obviously was never a victim of the Feast of Folly. And of course the Cappadocians could still Embrace.<br /> <br /> Looking at the material I can find on the Harbinders across the Editions, my headcanon is that some could Embrace but most couldn't and even among those that could, few did, either due to Lazarus' order or their own obsessions/madness. Further some of the Harbingers of Skull were not from the Feast of Folly but rather Cappadocians (mostly of Lazarus' Brood) that joined prior to the Family Reunion and they could still Embrace.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516349-v5-harbingers-not-entirely-sure-on-the-lore?p=1516947#post1516947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We should clear up what we're calling a &quot;Wraith-Harbinger&quot;.<br /> <br /> If we're talking about the old fucks that survived the Feast of Folly and kicked around in the Shadowlands for however long, that's absolutely a thing and it's pretty clear from past-edition lore they at least needed a corpse on this side of the Shroud to possess. They didn't have Nihilistics/Vitreous path initially to sustain themselves on wraiths, and once the initial supply ran out, that was it for them and they devolved. <i>How</i> that happened, and the implications it had for the Harbingers' existence (AKA, how they retained generation, disciplines, et cetera), was less clear-cut and this is the first time (I can recall) we got anything approaching mechanics for it.<br /> <br /> I know v20 has that band-aid solution about Harbingers sustaining themselves off the river Styx or however that worked, and of course there was always Enoch and its imported kine (which was always a bit silly if you ask me). But, those aren't all-encompassing solutions and v20 is best considered a side game/alternate timeline to v5 with its built-in metaplot agnosticism.<br /> <br /> Now, if we're talking about taking <i>actual</i> wraiths as opposed to disembodied vampires, that's where I'm looking in terms of Harbinger &quot;reproduction&quot;. If this is a thing they can just do now, it seems like it would be a preferable alternative to the embrace: you're getting a product already bound to you in a way not easily replicable without decades of thralldom and conditioning, in a package that isn't essentially a free meal for your enemies, without having to put your blood out there for anyone with sorcery to track and weaponize against you.<br /> <br /> <i>(Assuming the handful of discipline levels, sorcery paths, and rituals that allow for attacking a vampire's sire through blood sympathies ever get reprinted for v5...)</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure where you're getting this lore. As I said, Guide to the Sabbat regarded them as normal if ancient vampires. The V20 Rulebook was basically the same. Lore of the Bloodlines was kind of all over the place in that regard with the fluff section of their chapter being told by multiple different Harbingers with their own biases. Only one of them in one of the briefer sections reveals that and even they acknowledge that other Harbingers think they are mad. In fact the very next page of the book has a text box talking about how every Harbinger that spent prolonged periods in the Underworld suffer from mental trauma and damage so we can't even say that said Harbinger is actually a wraith or just insane*. Mechanically, unless the Half-Life merit is taken, a V20 Harbinger is a normal vampire. And given that it's a 6pt Merit, that kind of implies that it's on the rarer side. Plus other vampires don't like those kind of Harbingers as the merit states that if that condition is discovered, the vampire can expect to be hunted mercilessly. And I wouldn't be surprised if that included other Harbingers as they know first hand how terrible Wraiths can be, never mind one in the body of Vampire.<br /> <br /> So while I don't deny that such Wraith-Harbingers exist, I doubt they exist in great numbers. Again, a majority of pre-Family Reunion Harbingers are normal vampires, among which are the survivors of the Feast of Folly that escaped into the Underworld until Lazarus freed them.<br /> <br /> *It should also be noted that the Harbinger in question is the Wearer of the Pantalone Mask which also doesn't exactly paint their words in a good light as it's a comedic figure that is frequently the butt of jokes. Now it's possible that the Harbinger in question is aware of the meaning behind the name and is intentionally wearing it as a masquerade but at the same time as far as I'm aware, that is section is the only time we've seen this Harbinger. On the other hand, Khurshid, the Harbinger who starts their chapter and has the longest section in it, is a real character who would appear in Beckett's Jyhad Diary. And he is a real vampire so it again paints the picture that most Harbringers are normal vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T10:17:16-07:00","id":1517082,"title":"","content":"I was always curious what the plan was after Beckett's for the Corpse Families. The purported 4E Vampire would have probably invested a lot of time in exploring and building up this plotline and how it would develop for these <i>lovely </i>folks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-06T01:55:16-07:00","id":1517253,"title":"","content":"Yep! I created / wrangled / condensed all that lore for Cults of the Blood Gods because I wasn't anticipating any books covering metaplot in the future. I don't believe I was wrong in that estimate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-06T08:29:57-07:00","id":1517278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516349-v5-harbingers-not-entirely-sure-on-the-lore?p=1517253#post1517253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep! I created / wrangled / condensed all that lore for Cults of the Blood Gods because I wasn't anticipating any books covering metaplot in the future. I don't believe I was wrong in that estimate.</div> </div> </div> </div>For what it's worth, it's actually my favorite post-v20 metaplot development. It's nice actually seeing <i>someone</i> actually trying to create something new, even if that something is objectively terrible.<br /> <br /> Also the idea of Lazarus running around like a millenia-old blues brother, going &quot;were getting the band back together&quot; is hilarious to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-06T08:37:15-07:00","id":1517282,"title":"","content":"As I put it with the Hecate is that desperate times call for strange alliances if it means to better there chances at survival with the upheaval in the realms of the dead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-06T10:38:19-07:00","id":1517291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516349-v5-harbingers-not-entirely-sure-on-the-lore?p=1517253#post1517253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep! I created / wrangled / condensed all that lore for Cults of the Blood Gods because I wasn't anticipating any books covering metaplot in the future. I don't believe I was wrong in that estimate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well.... that sucks. I figured it, but to hear it outright from one of the writers hits hard. I know you might be limited in ability to answer, but can you share why you have that estimate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5617-vendrin","name":"Vendrin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-06T23:14:31-07:00","id":1517332,"title":"","content":"I base my estimate on the trend of releases and awareness of direction I was given as a developer. That said, things can always change. Renegade could announce the big book of metaplot tomorrow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-07T07:58:35-07:00","id":1517355,"title":"","content":"Thanks for your reply!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5617-vendrin","name":"Vendrin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}